 "notes": "HAYSTAC Phase II haloscope, axion-photon coupling. Headline limit = combined Phase II exclusion over 16.96-19.46 ueV at 90% CL; paper quotes per-frequency 10% prior-update contours plus aggregate |g_gamma|>=2.86 x g_KSVZ (Phase IIc 2.96x over 18.71-19.46 ueV, Phase IId 2.75x over 17.28-18.44 ueV). Curve extracted from Fig.3 bottom-left panel (vector PDF HAYSTAC_PIIExc.pdf) as the lower edge (limit) of the blue (PII-ab) + magenta (PII-cd) excluded fills, per-column, binned to ~90 pts (gaps at mode crossings 17.89-18.08 & 18.13-18.18 ueV and RFI notches dropped). y-axis native |g_gamma/g_KSVZ|; converted to g_agamma via g_agamma = value * g_gamma^KSVZ*alpha/(pi*f_a), f_a=Lambda^2/m_a, Lambda=77.6 MeV, g_gamma^KSVZ=0.97 => g_KSVZ=3.742e-10 * m_a[eV] GeV^-1. Extracted per-freq limit reaches down to ~1x KSVZ, max ~2.84x matching the stated aggregate 2.86. DM density rho_a=0.45 GeV/cm^3 (not rescaled). Phase I orange 23-24 ueV in Fig.3 is previously published (Backes 2021), not this new result.",
